WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.362
Where are agencies?

2
00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:05.403
Learn's known limitations page
covers the whole product:

3
00:00:05.403 --> 00:00:08.326
Global Secure Access
is available in G C C.

4
00:00:08.326 --> 00:00:12.218
No feature page read for the
guide narrows or widens that,

5
00:00:12.218 --> 00:00:15.200
so the G C C column rests
on that one sentence.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.537
A preview feature, such as the cloud
firewall for clients or the Explicit Forward

7
00:00:20.537 --> 00:00:24.122
Proxy, has a G C C availability
that is not yet specified,

8
00:00:24.122 --> 00:00:27.388
and the guide adopts one
only by a decision record.

9
00:00:27.388 --> 00:00:30.557
The table is as of
November eleventh, 2026,

10
00:00:30.557 --> 00:00:34.287
so re-read the limitations
page before each ring.

11
00:00:34.287 --> 00:00:39.731
And where a row of the decision record
says retain the current service, or defer,

12
00:00:39.731 --> 00:00:45.342
it names its compensating controls: for
example, the current fed-ramp authorized

13
00:00:45.342 --> 00:00:50.760
S S E, per-application V P N access lists,
and named-location Conditional Access.
